{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/769918-your-houserules-for-2nd-edition","id":769918,"title":"Your Houserules for 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-20T06:19:02-08:00","id":769918,"title":"Your Houserules for 2nd Edition","content":"Let's admit it, no matter how good the base rules are (and I've found that Werewolf has turned from my least favourite WoD game to be in my Top 2, so kudos to the team!) each group, Storyteller and players have their own particularities that led themselves to tweaks, some small, others bigger.<br /> <br /> So, wich houserules have you decided to add to your Forsaken 2nd edition games and why?<br /> <br /> As is only polite, I'll start:<br /> <br /> <b>Gift and Facets initial distribution: </b>One of the things I liked the most about NWoD and specially 2nd edition was the consistency in the cost of traits at any point in the game, both at character creation and later. That's why the initial number of Facets and Renown that the game has by default felt a little off.<br /> <br /> Normally each dot of Renown would grant you an appropiate Facet of a Shadow Gift, Auspice Renown would also give you a Facet of a Moon Gift on top of that. So far, so good.<br /> But! A regular character receives 3 dots of Renown (one from Auspice, one from Tribe and one Free Pick) yet only 2 Shadow Gift Facets. I decided to up this number to three Facets while keeping the number of Shadow Gifts unlocked to 2. Ghost Wolves having only 2 dots of Renown only get 2 Facets, they also only Unlock one Shadow Gift among their Auspice list.<br /> <br /> <b>Gauru Bonuses distribution: </b>Seeing no much use to that vestigial +1 to Dexterity and wanting forms to be more distinct (the current distribution is too close to that of Urshul for my taste) I decided to move that extra dot to Strength. That way I have the added benefit, from my point of view, of having even an average human having literally superhuman strength (6) while in Gauru.<br /> <br /> So, what about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:28:25-08:00","id":769922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/769918-your-houserules-for-2nd-edition#post769918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing no much use to that vestigial +1 to Dexterity</div> </div> </div> </div>It's for throwing shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:30:52-08:00","id":769925,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was the only thing I came up with. Great Strenght allows to lift and throw a lot of things, but the roll is still Dexterity+Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:36:25-08:00","id":769932,"title":"","content":"We've added <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-3-weapons-and-equipment/\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker's Bleeding Tilt</a> to the list of effects a werewolf can inflict on someone with their Weaken the Prey urshul ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hurt Locker Open Development</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleeding (Firearms or bladed weapons)<br /> The character bleeds profusely from an open wound. If she doesn't staunch the blood flow, she may soon pass out from shock and blood loss. <br /> Effect: Bleeding characters suffer a -1 wound penalty (or have existing wound penalties increased in severity by 1). Additionally, each turn that she remains bleeding, she suffers one automatic point of bashing damage. <br /> Causing the Tilt: Firearms or bladed weapons that score more damage in a single attack than the victim's Stamina inflict this Tilt. The attacker must make a general attack, rather than targeting the victim for a called shot. <br /> Ending the Tilt: If the character takes a turn to apply pressure and some sort of cloth or tie a tourniquet around the bleeding limb, she can stop the flow of blood and end the Tilt. Any form of accelerated healing, even a single bashing level, will stop the bleeding as well. For obvious reasons, the undead are immune to this Tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:39:05-08:00","id":769935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/769918-your-houserules-for-2nd-edition?p=769932#post769932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've added <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-3-weapons-and-equipment/\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker's Bleeding Tilt</a> to the list of effects a werewolf can inflict on someone with their Weaken the Prey urshul ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice one, I'll add it to my repertoire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:02:49-08:00","id":769994,"title":"","content":"Binding spirits in 2.0 suffers a flat penalty equal to the spirit's rank. I instead compare the ranks of the spirit and ritualist, and the difference in favor with them, like back in 1.0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:56:50-08:00","id":773297,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else do anything about the Tribe/Auspice combinations that only receive four Shadow Gifts in-Affinity instead of five? It's really only a difference of two Experiences overall. Compared to 2E Disciplines, in which bumping an out-of-Clan to five is an extra five Experiences on top, it's not terrible. Do you make acquiring the out-of-Affinity Gifts commensurately more difficult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4392-vaermithrax","name":"vaermithrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:35:53-08:00","id":773341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/769918-your-houserules-for-2nd-edition?p=769932#post769932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've added <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-open-dev-dump-3-weapons-and-equipment/\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker's Bleeding Tilt</a> to the list of effects a werewolf can inflict on someone with their Weaken the Prey urshul ability.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I originally tried to add a number of new Tilts to Forsaken, especially due to the new Urshul\u200b capability, but sadly didn't get the wordcount for it. They included one for inflicting a bleeding wound, one for crippling a target's natural weaponry, one for cracking open armour and a few other bits and pieces (including potentially more esoteric ones that attacked Essence, etc).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:49:27-08:00","id":773349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/769918-your-houserules-for-2nd-edition?p=773341#post773341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I originally tried to add a number of new Tilts to Forsaken, especially due to the new Urshul\u200b capability, but sadly didn't get the wordcount for it. They included one for inflicting a bleeding wound, one for crippling a target's natural weaponry, one for cracking open armour and a few other bits and pieces (including potentially more esoteric ones that attacked Essence, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>So cool. I'm hoping at some point we get some Poison or Toxin gifts so we can inflict poison with a bite. Maybe a Merit could do it, like Markov's Toxic Familiar from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane. I really like the idea of werewolves becoming more 'naturally' customized, not just through the use of Essence. The passive facets and Favored and Fortified Form merits are great for that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4392-vaermithrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4392\" data-vbnamecard=\"4392\">vaermithrax</a> I believe there's mention of some houserules in another thread but I'm not sure which. I personally don't mind it, but I know some people prefer an equality standpoint for these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}